  "notes": "{陶酔|とうすい} contains {陶|とう} (pottery/to mold) and {酔|すい} (drunk), suggesting being shaped or molded by the experience of intoxication.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {陶酔|とうすい}する: to be intoxicated, to be enraptured\n- ～に{陶酔|とうすい}する: to be intoxicated by ~\n- {自己|じこ}{陶酔|とうすい}: self-intoxication, narcissism\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {酔|よ}う: to get drunk (more literal)\n- {恍惚|こうこつ}: ecstasy (more intense)\n- {夢中|むちゅう}: absorbed in (less intense)",
